<header><h1>The Arborec: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_arborec">The Arborec</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it. <b>Reasoning</b> shows how a note no source addresses follows from the card text and rules.</p>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Mitosis">Mitosis</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Arborec player produces units with both a space dock and Letani Warriors in the same system, any infantry they produce must be placed on a planet that contains a Letani Warrior.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Vidyaraja, Sep 18, 2017): &ldquo;Letani Warriors in the same system can pool their production. You can use them to produce infantry in the way that you described (though the infantry must be placed on a planet that has a Letani Warrior on it).&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Arborec infantry Production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Arborec space docks can never produce infantry, so infantry output is capped by the Letani Warriors&rsquo; own Production.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Arborec player may produce <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Mech:~:text=Letani%20Behemoth">Letani Behemoth</a> with their space docks.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Arborec infantry Production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Arborec space docks can never produce infantry.&rdquo; Mechs are not infantry.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Stymie">Stymie</a> (replaced by &Omega;) <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>10</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>10</sup> Codex I p. 8, &ldquo;The Omega Initiative&rdquo;: &ldquo;Components from this section replace preexisting components of the same name and type.&rdquo; The Omega Initiative contents (p. 3) list &ldquo;Stymie&rdquo;.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Stymie</i> is returned when the system is activated, even if the active player will perform no hostile acts toward the Arborec player this turn.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Stymie: &ldquo;If you activate a system that contains 1 or more of the Arborec player&rsquo;s units, return this card to the Arborec player.&rdquo; Activation alone triggers it; the card mentions no movement, combat or other hostile act.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Activating a system containing only the Arborec player&rsquo;s structures will still cause <i>Stymie</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Stymie returns when a player activates a system &ldquo;that contains 1 or more of the Arborec player&rsquo;s units.&rdquo; LRR 85: &ldquo;A structure is a type of unit.&rdquo; A system with only Arborec structures contains Arborec units.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an effect other than activating a system during a tactical action places a command token in a system with the Arborec player&rsquo;s units (for example, the primary ability of the <i>Diplomacy</i> strategy card), this will not cause <i>Stymie</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: LRR 5.1: &ldquo;When a player performs a tactical action, they activate a system by placing a command token from their tactic pool in that system.&rdquo; Stymie returns only &ldquo;if you activate a system&rdquo;; a token placed by another effect activates nothing.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Stymie">Stymie &Omega;</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Stymie</i> cannot place a command token in the home system of an eliminated player.<sup>2,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Arborec Stymie note stop the Arborec from producing in their home system?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Stymie only covers non-home systems containing the holder&rsquo;s units and the systems adjacent to them.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, &ldquo;What happens to Avernus if Muaat is eliminated?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Avernus, its token, planet card and legendary ability remain in play. Similar to an eliminated faction&rsquo;s home system.&rdquo; An eliminated player&rsquo;s home system stays a home system.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Bioplasmosis">Bioplasmosis</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>No infantry may move beyond an adjacent system. For example, consider a series of systems A&ndash;B&ndash;C. Only systems connected by a &ldquo;&ndash;&rdquo; are adjacent. In this case:<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Bioplasmosis or Transit Diodes move ground forces onto enemy planets, or chain across systems?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Bioplasmosis moves each infantry once, to a planet in its own or an adjacent system, so no hopping across several systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>An infantry cannot move from A to B, then B to C.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Bioplasmosis or Transit Diodes move ground forces onto enemy planets, or chain across systems?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Bioplasmosis moves each infantry once, to a planet in its own or an adjacent system, so no hopping across several systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>An infantry may move from A to B, while another infantry moves from B to C.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Bioplasmosis moves each infantry once.&rdquo; Each infantry moves separately.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>An infantry may move from A to B, while another infantry moves from C to B.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Bioplasmosis moves each infantry once.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>An infantry may move from B to A, while another infantry moves from B to C.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Bioplasmosis moves each infantry once.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>An infantry may move from A to B, while another infantry moves from B to A. This will have no meaningful effect.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Bioplasmosis: &ldquo;remove any number of infantry from planets you control and place them on 1 or more planets you control in the same or adjacent systems.&rdquo; After the swap each planet holds one infantry, as before.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li><i>Bioplasmosis</i> cannot move <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Mech:~:text=Letani%20Behemoth">Letani Behemoth</a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Bioplasmosis moves only &ldquo;infantry&rdquo;. LRR 55: &ldquo;Mechs are unique, faction-specific heavy ground forces.&rdquo; A mech is a ground force, not an infantry.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Infantry:~:text=Letani%20Warrior">Letani Warrior</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When multiple units use their <sc>Production</sc> ability, the <sc>Production</sc> value is pooled. As such, if the Arborec player has two Letani Warrior I in a system, they may produce two infantry for one resource, rather than two.<sup>1,2,3,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the &lsquo;Production&rsquo; abilities of multiple Arborec &lsquo;Letani Warriors&rsquo; in a system be combined to allow the production of two infantry for one resource? A: Yes. Production value is totaled when the &lsquo;Production&rsquo; ability of units in a system is used.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;Their Production pools with your other units in the system.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Letani Warriors in the same system can pool their production.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;When producing multiple units at a time, the cost values of those units are added together.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If Letani Warriors are on different planets, any produced ground forces may be split between those planets, regardless of the production value of the Letani Warriors on that planet.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Where are produced ground forces placed?&rdquo;: &ldquo;With several producing planets you may split them among those planets however you like, even all on one.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the infantry must be placed on a planet that has a Letani Warrior on it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Flagship:~:text=Duha%20Menaimon">Duha Menaimon</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The produced units must be paid for.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When an ability other than &lsquo;Production&rsquo; allows you to produce one or more units, do you have to pay for the units produced? A: Yes, a unit that is produced must always be paid for.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal on Integrated Economy (a similar non-Production effect): &ldquo;paid normally.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Duha Menaimon</i> does not have <sc>Production</sc>. As such, the <i>Sarween Tools</i> technology and similar such effects do not apply to the <i>Duha Menaimon</i>.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When producing a unit with an ability other than &lsquo;Production,&rsquo; does the price reduction from the &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; technology apply? A: No, &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; is only used with the &lsquo;Production&rsquo; ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <i>Duha Menaimon</i> must be in the system when it is activated for its effect to trigger. It will not trigger if it is moved into the active system later in the turn.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Does the Arborec flagship (The &lsquo;Duha Menaimon&rsquo;) need to be in a system when it is activated &hellip;? A: Yes. The &lsquo;Duha Menaimon&rsquo; can only be used to produce units when it is in a system at the moment it is activated.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When does the Arborec flagship produce, and can it move in first?&rdquo;: &ldquo;so it only works if it is already in the active system; it can&rsquo;t move in and then produce&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Leaders:~:text=Letani%20Ospha">Letani Ospha</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The replaced ship is not destroyed. The replacing ship is not produced.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Letani Ospha: &ldquo;that player may replace that ship with one from their reinforcements.&rdquo; The card replaces the ship; it does not destroy it, and it spends no resources, which LRR 67.1 requires to produce a unit: &ldquo;To produce a unit, a player must spend a number of resources.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The <i>Sarween Tools</i> technology and similar effects will not allow a more expensive ship to be placed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Sarween Tools: &ldquo;When 1 or more of your units use PRODUCTION, reduce the combined cost of the produced units by 1.&rdquo; Letani Ospha uses no PRODUCTION and produces nothing; &ldquo;costs up to 2 more than the replaced ship&rdquo; compares printed costs.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the player wishes to place a ship, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a ship of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This ship will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A fighter may be placed with Letani Ospha.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Letani Ospha requires only the chosen ship to be &ldquo;non-fighter&rdquo;; the new ship is any &ldquo;one from their reinforcements that costs up to 2 more.&rdquo; LRR 76: &ldquo;A ship is a unit type consisting of carriers, cruisers, dreadnoughts, destroyers, fighters, and war suns.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Leaders:~:text=Dirzuga%20Rophal">Dirzuga Rophal</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The produced unit must be paid for.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When an ability other than &lsquo;Production&rsquo; allows you to produce one or more units, do you have to pay for the units produced? A: Yes, a unit that is produced must always be paid for.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Saar&rsquo;s Chaos Mapping production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;you still pay for it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A ship may be produced only if no other player currently has ships in that system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: LRR 67.6: &ldquo;A player cannot produce ships in a system that contains other players&rsquo; ships.&rdquo; Dirzuga Rophal produces &ldquo;1 unit in that system,&rdquo; so this limit applies.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>No unit is using its <sc>Production</sc> ability. The <i>Sarween Tools</i> technology and similar effects will not apply.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When producing a unit with an ability other than &lsquo;Production,&rsquo; does the price reduction from the &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; technology apply? A: No, &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; is only used with the &lsquo;Production&rsquo; ability.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Sarween Tools work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It needs a unit&rsquo;s Production ability, so it doesn&rsquo;t apply to effects that just let you produce.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Arborec player may produce an infantry, even if the only unit with the <sc>Production</sc> ability in the active system is their space dock.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: LRR 68.1d: &ldquo;&rsquo;Production&rsquo; value from Arborec space docks cannot be used to produce infantry.&rdquo; Dirzuga Rophal uses no PRODUCTION value: the space dock only meets the trigger (&ldquo;a system that contains 1 or more of your units that have PRODUCTION&rdquo;), then &ldquo;You may produce 1 unit in that system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Arborec player wishes to place a unit, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a unit of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This unit will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;When a player wishes to produce a unit but has no units of that type available in their reinforcements, that player may remove one of their units of that type from a system that does not contain one of their command tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A unit with <sc>Production</sc> in an entropic scar still has <sc>Production</sc>, even though it cannot use it. As such, Dirzuga Rophal may still be used in that system.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the Arborec commander work with a Letani in an Entropic Scar?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; the scar stops unit abilities being used but doesn&rsquo;t remove them, and the commander is a text ability that only needs a unit with Production.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Leaders:~:text=Letani%20Miasmiala">Letani Miasmiala</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Leaders:~:text=Ultrasonic%20Emitter">Ultrasonic Emitter</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The produced units must all be paid for.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When an ability other than &lsquo;Production&rsquo; allows you to produce one or more units, do you have to pay for the units produced? A: Yes, a unit that is produced must always be paid for.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A ship may be produced in the system only if no other player currently has ships in that system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: LRR 67.6: &ldquo;A player cannot produce ships in a system that contains other players&rsquo; ships.&rdquo; Ultrasonic Emitter produces units &ldquo;in any number of systems,&rdquo; so this limit applies in each.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>No unit is using its <sc>Production</sc> ability. The <i>Sarween Tools</i> technology and similar effects will not apply.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;When producing a unit with an ability other than &lsquo;Production,&rsquo; does the price reduction from the &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; technology apply? A: No, &lsquo;Sarween Tools&rsquo; is only used with the &lsquo;Production&rsquo; ability.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Sarween Tools work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It needs a unit&rsquo;s Production ability, so it doesn&rsquo;t apply to effects that just let you produce.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a ground force is produced in a system, it may be placed on any planet the Arborec player controls in that system, regardless of what units, if any, the Arborec player has on that planet. The produced ground force may also be placed in the space area of that system.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Reasoning</b>: Ultrasonic Emitter: &ldquo;Produce any number of units in any number of systems that contain 1 or more of your ground forces.&rdquo; LRR 67.4b: &ldquo;If an ability allows a player to produce a unit in a system, they may produce that unit in the space area or on a planet they control in that system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Arborec#Mech:~:text=Letani%20Behemoth">Letani Behemoth</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Arborec player may produce Letani Behemoth with their space docks.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Arborec infantry Production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Arborec space docks can never produce infantry.&rdquo; Mechs are not infantry.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

